          tileFixedCount σ d ^ (n / d)

/-- For even `n`, the square-torus `r²f` formula is multiplied by two.  Its power-dependent
fixed count is `tileFixedCount σ d = t_{(r²f)^d}` and the design permutation satisfies `σ²=1`.

Formalization deviation: none beyond the representation choices stated above.

Source: Peter Kagey, William Keehn, *Counting Tilings of the n × m Grid, Cylinder, and Torus*,
        Journal of Integer Sequences 27 (2024), Article 24.6.1, Theorem 38. -/
public theorem_wanted squareTorus_r2f_even {T : Type*} [Fintype T] [DecidableEq T]
    (n : ℕ) [NeZero n] (σ : Equiv.Perm T) (hσ : σ ^ 2 = 1) (hn : Even n) :
    2 * torusShiftSum n n (cellR2F n n) σ =
      n * ∑ d ∈ n.divisors, Nat.totient d *
        (Fintype.card T ^ (n ^ 2 / Nat.lcm 2 d) +
          Fintype.card T ^ ((n ^ 2 - 2 * n) / Nat.lcm 2 d) *
            tileFixedCount σ d ^ (2 * n / d))

/-- For odd `n`, the square-torus `r²f` formula is the divisor sum with fixed-design term
`tileFixedCount σ d = t_{(r²f)^d}`.  The hypothesis `σ²=1` records the reflection order.

Formalization deviation: none beyond the representation choices stated above.

Source: Peter Kagey, William Keehn, *Counting Tilings of the n × m Grid, Cylinder, and Torus*,
        Journal of Integer Sequences 27 (2024), Article 24.6.1, Theorem 38. -/
public theorem_wanted squareTorus_r2f_odd {T : Type*} [Fintype T] [DecidableEq T]
    (n : ℕ) [NeZero n] (σ : Equiv.Perm T) (hσ : σ ^ 2 = 1) (hn : Odd n) :
    torusShiftSum n n (cellR2F n n) σ =
      n * ∑ d ∈ n.divisors, Nat.totient d *
        Fintype.card T ^ ((n ^ 2 - n) / Nat.lcm 2 d) *
          tileFixedCount σ d ^ (n / d)

/-- For odd `n`, the square-torus quarter-turn `r` shift-sum is
`n²t_id^((n²-1)/4)t_r`.  The term `tileFixedCount σ 1` is `t_r`, and `σ⁴=1` is the rotation's
order hypothesis for every tile action.

Formalization deviation: none beyond the representation choices stated above.

Source: Peter Kagey, William Keehn, *Counting Tilings of the n × m Grid, Cylinder, and Torus*,
        Journal of Integer Sequences 27 (2024), Article 24.6.1, Theorem 39. -/
public theorem_wanted squareTorus_r_odd {T : Type*} [Fintype T] [DecidableEq T]
    (n : ℕ) [NeZero n] (σ : Equiv.Perm T) (hσ : σ ^ 4 = 1) (hn : Odd n) :
    torusShiftSum n n (cellR n) σ =
      n ^ 2 * Fintype.card T ^ ((n ^ 2 - 1) / 4) * tileFixedCount σ 1

/-- For even `n`, the `r` square-torus formula is multiplied through by two.  The second term
contains `t_r²t_{r²}`, encoded by `(tileFixedCount σ 1)² * tileFixedCount σ 2`; `σ⁴=1` records
the quarter-turn order.

Formalization deviation: none beyond the representation choices stated above.

Source: Peter Kagey, William Keehn, *Counting Tilings of the n × m Grid, Cylinder, and Torus*,
        Journal of Integer Sequences 27 (2024), Article 24.6.1, Theorem 39. -/
public theorem_wanted squareTorus_r_even {T : Type*} [Fintype T] [DecidableEq T]
    (n : ℕ) [NeZero n] (σ : Equiv.Perm T) (hσ : σ ^ 4 = 1) (hn : Even n) :
    2 * torusShiftSum n n (cellR n) σ =
      n ^ 2 * (Fintype.card T ^ (n ^ 2 / 4) +
        Fintype.card T ^ ((n ^ 2 - 4) / 4) *
          tileFixedCount σ 1 ^ 2 * tileFixedCount σ 2)

/-- The odd-`n` `r³` square-torus formula equals the corresponding `r` formula.  It is stated
with the actual cell map and its own permutation `σ`, whose fourth power is the identity;
`tileFixedCount σ 1` is the fixed count of the represented `r³` action.

Formalization deviation: none beyond the representation choices stated above.

Source: Peter Kagey, William Keehn, *Counting Tilings of the n × m Grid, Cylinder, and Torus*,
        Journal of Integer Sequences 27 (2024), Article 24.6.1, Theorem 39. -/
public theorem_wanted squareTorus_r3_odd {T : Type*} [Fintype T] [DecidableEq T]
    (n : ℕ) [NeZero n] (σ : Equiv.Perm T) (hσ : σ ^ 4 = 1) (hn : Odd n) :
    torusShiftSum n n (cellR3 n) σ =
      n ^ 2 * Fintype.card T ^ ((n ^ 2 - 1) / 4) * tileFixedCount σ 1

/-- The even-`n` `r³` formula is separately stated and multiplied by two.  Its fixed counts for
the first and second powers are `tileFixedCount σ 1` and `tileFixedCount σ 2`, and the tile
permutation satisfies the appropriate fourth-power identity.

Formalization deviation: none beyond the representation choices stated above.

Source: Peter Kagey, William Keehn, *Counting Tilings of the n × m Grid, Cylinder, and Torus*,
        Journal of Integer Sequences 27 (2024), Article 24.6.1, Theorem 39. -/
public theorem_wanted squareTorus_r3_even {T : Type*} [Fintype T] [DecidableEq T]
    (n : ℕ) [NeZero n] (σ : Equiv.Perm T) (hσ : σ ^ 4 = 1) (hn : Even n) :
    2 * torusShiftSum n n (cellR3 n) σ =
      n ^ 2 * (Fintype.card T ^ (n ^ 2 / 4) +
        Fintype.card T ^ ((n ^ 2 - 4) / 4) *
          tileFixedCount σ 1 ^ 2 * tileFixedCount σ 2)

/-- The `rf` square-torus shift-sum is split into sums over odd and even divisors rather than a
piecewise summand.  Odd `d` contributes the `t_rf^(n/d)` factor, while even `d` contributes only
`t_id`; `σ²=1` is the reflection-order hypothesis.  This is algebraically the paper's Theorem 40.

Formalization deviation: none beyond the representation choices stated above.

Source: Peter Kagey, William Keehn, *Counting Tilings of the n × m Grid, Cylinder, and Torus*,
        Journal of Integer Sequences 27 (2024), Article 24.6.1, Theorem 40. -/
public theorem_wanted squareTorus_rf {T : Type*} [Fintype T] [DecidableEq T]
    (n : ℕ) [NeZero n] (σ : Equiv.Perm T) (hσ : σ ^ 2 = 1) :
    torusShiftSum n n (cellRF n) σ = n *
      ((∑ d ∈ n.divisors.filter Odd,
          Nat.totient d * Fintype.card T ^ ((n ^ 2 - n) / (2 * d)) *
            tileFixedCount σ 1 ^ (n / d)) +
        ∑ d ∈ n.divisors.filter Even,
          Nat.totient d * Fintype.card T ^ (n ^ 2 / (2 * d)))

/-- The `r³f` square-torus formula has the same odd/even divisor split as `rf`, with the actual
`cellR3F` map and `t_{r³f}` represented by `tileFixedCount σ 1`.  The hypothesis `σ²=1` records
the reflection order on every tile set.

Formalization deviation: none beyond the representation choices stated above.

Source: Peter Kagey, William Keehn, *Counting Tilings of the n × m Grid, Cylinder, and Torus*,
        Journal of Integer Sequences 27 (2024), Article 24.6.1, Theorem 40. -/
public theorem_wanted squareTorus_r3f {T : Type*} [Fintype T] [DecidableEq T]
    (n : ℕ) [NeZero n] (σ : Equiv.Perm T) (hσ : σ ^ 2 = 1) :
    torusShiftSum n n (cellR3F n) σ = n *
      ((∑ d ∈ n.divisors.filter Odd,
          Nat.totient d * Fintype.card T ^ ((n ^ 2 - n) / (2 * d)) *
            tileFixedCount σ 1 ^ (n / d)) +
        ∑ d ∈ n.divisors.filter Even,
          Nat.totient d * Fintype.card T ^ (n ^ 2 / (2 * d)))


/-- The cell maps of the paper's rectangle symmetry group `D₄ = ⟨r², f⟩` on the `n × m` grid,
indexed by Mathlib's `DihedralGroup 4` with `f = sr 0` and `r² = r 2` (so `r²f = sr 2`):
`r 0 ↦ id`, `r 2 ↦ cellR2`, `sr 0 ↦ cellF`, `sr 2 ↦ cellR2F`. On this subgroup `g ↦ cell map`
is a homomorphism into maps under composition. The other four elements (not in the rectangle
group) get the values `cellR2` (`r 1`, `r 3`) and `cellR2F` (`sr 1`, `sr 3`), which are never used.

Source: Peter Kagey, William Keehn, *Counting Tilings of the n × m Grid, Cylinder, and Torus*,
        Journal of Integer Sequences 27 (2024), Article 24.6.1, Definitions 1.4.1 and 1.4.2 (the
        dihedral action on cells). -/
public def rectCellAction (n m : ℕ) : DihedralGroup 4 → ZMod n × ZMod m → ZMod n × ZMod m
  | .r i => if i = 0 then id else cellR2 n m
  | .sr i => if i = 0 then cellF n m else cellR2F n m

/-- `r 0` acts on cells as the identity.

Source: Peter Kagey, William Keehn, *Counting Tilings of the n × m Grid, Cylinder, and Torus*,
        Journal of Integer Sequences 27 (2024), Article 24.6.1, Definition 1.4.1. -/
public theorem rectCellAction_r_zero (n m : ℕ) : rectCellAction n m (.r 0) = id := rfl

/-- `r 2` acts on cells as the half-turn `cellR2`.

Source: Peter Kagey, William Keehn, *Counting Tilings of the n × m Grid, Cylinder, and Torus*,
        Journal of Integer Sequences 27 (2024), Article 24.6.1, Definition 1.4.1. -/
public theorem rectCellAction_r_two (n m : ℕ) : rectCellAction n m (.r 2) = cellR2 n m := by
  simp [rectCellAction, show (2 : ZMod 4) ≠ 0 by decide]

/-- `sr 0` acts on cells as the reflection `f`, `cellF`.

Source: Peter Kagey, William Keehn, *Counting Tilings of the n × m Grid, Cylinder, and Torus*,
        Journal of Integer Sequences 27 (2024), Article 24.6.1, Definition 1.4.1. -/
public theorem rectCellAction_sr_zero (n m : ℕ) : rectCellAction n m (.sr 0) = cellF n m := rfl

/-- `sr 2` acts on cells as `r²f`, `cellR2F`.

Source: Peter Kagey, William Keehn, *Counting Tilings of the n × m Grid, Cylinder, and Torus*,
        Journal of Integer Sequences 27 (2024), Article 24.6.1, Definition 1.4.1. -/
public theorem rectCellAction_sr_two (n m : ℕ) : rectCellAction n m (.sr 2) = cellR2F n m := by
  simp [rectCellAction, show (2 : ZMod 4) ≠ 0 by decide]

/-- The cell maps of the paper's square symmetry group `D₈ = ⟨r, f⟩` on the `n × n` grid, indexed
by Mathlib's `DihedralGroup 4`: `r i ↦ rⁱ` and `sr i ↦ f ∘ rⁱ` with `r = cellR` and `f = cellF`.
Since `f r f = r⁻¹` on cells, `g ↦ squareCellAction n g` is a homomorphism into maps under
composition for Mathlib's multiplication.

Source: Peter Kagey, William Keehn, *Counting Tilings of the n × m Grid, Cylinder, and Torus*,
        Journal of Integer Sequences 27 (2024), Article 24.6.1, Definition 1.4.2 (the dihedral
        action on cells). -/
public def squareCellAction (n : ℕ) : DihedralGroup 4 → ZMod n × ZMod n → ZMod n × ZMod n
  | .r i => (cellR n)^[i.val]
  | .sr i => cellF n n ∘ (cellR n)^[i.val]

/-- `r 1` acts on square-grid cells as the quarter-turn `cellR`.

Source: Peter Kagey, William Keehn, *Counting Tilings of the n × m Grid, Cylinder, and Torus*,
        Journal of Integer Sequences 27 (2024), Article 24.6.1, Definition 1.4.2. -/
public theorem squareCellAction_r_one (n : ℕ) : squareCellAction n (.r 1) = cellR n := rfl

/-- `sr 0` acts on square-grid cells as the reflection `cellF`.

Source: Peter Kagey, William Keehn, *Counting Tilings of the n × m Grid, Cylinder, and Torus*,
        Journal of Integer Sequences 27 (2024), Article 24.6.1, Definition 1.4.2. -/
public theorem squareCellAction_sr_zero (n : ℕ) : squareCellAction n (.sr 0) = cellF n n := rfl

/-- Theorem 32 (Theorem 3.1.6 of the arXiv version): for a set of tile designs `T` with an
action of the symmetry group and a subgroup `R` of the rectangle group `D₄ = ⟨r², f⟩`, the number
of distinct tilings of the `n × m` cylinder is `(1/(n|R|)) ∑_{g ∈ R} fxpt^C_g(n,m)`, where
`fxpt^C_g(n,m) = cylinderShiftSum n m (rectCellAction n m g) (g • ·)` sums the fixed tilings of
`(a, g)` over the column shifts `a ∈ ℤ/nℤ`. Tilings are maps `ZMod n × ZMod m → T`; "distinct"
means up to the transformations `F ↦ (c ↦ g⁻¹ • F (g · (c + (a, 0))))`, `a ∈ ℤ/nℤ`, `g ∈ R`, which
fix `F` exactly when `F (g · (c + (a, 0))) = g • F c`, the fixed-point condition of
`cylinderShiftSum`. As in the paper, the tile designs form an `R`-set: the action is a
`MulAction R T` of the subgroup only, and `g ∈ R` acts on cells through its coercion.

Source: Peter Kagey, William Keehn, *Counting Tilings of the n × m Grid, Cylinder, and Torus*,
        Journal of Integer Sequences 27 (2024), Article 24.6.1, Theorem 32
        (`jis-2024-24.6.1-thm-32`). -/
public theorem_wanted cylinder_distinctTilings_burnside {T : Type*} [Fintype T] [DecidableEq T]
    (n m : ℕ) [NeZero n] [NeZero m]
    (R : Subgroup (DihedralGroup 4)) [DecidablePred (· ∈ R)] [MulAction R T]
    (hR : ∀ g ∈ R, g = .r 0 ∨ g = .r 2 ∨ g = .sr 0 ∨ g = .sr 2) :
    (Nat.card (Quot fun F F' : ZMod n × ZMod m → T =>
        ∃ a : ZMod n, ∃ g : R, ∀ c, F' c = g⁻¹ • F (rectCellAction n m g (c.1 + a, c.2))) : ℚ) =
      1 / (n * Nat.card R) * ∑ g : R,
        (cylinderShiftSum n m (rectCellAction n m g) (MulAction.toPerm g : Equiv.Perm T) : ℚ)

/-- Theorem 37 (Theorem 4.1.5 of the arXiv version): for a subgroup `R` of the rectangle group
`D₄ = ⟨r², f⟩`, the number of distinct tilings of the `n × m` torus is
`(1/(nm|R|)) ∑_{g ∈ R} fxpt^{RT}_g(n,m)`, where
`fxpt^{RT}_g(n,m) = torusShiftSum n m (rectCellAction n m g) (g • ·)` sums the fixed tilings of
`((a, b), g)` over the shifts `(a, b) ∈ ℤ/nℤ × ℤ/mℤ`. "Distinct" means up to the transformations
`F ↦ (c ↦ g⁻¹ • F (g · (c + v)))`, `v ∈ ℤ/nℤ × ℤ/mℤ`, `g ∈ R`, as in
`cylinder_distinctTilings_burnside`; the tile designs form an `R`-set (`MulAction R T`).

Source: Peter Kagey, William Keehn, *Counting Tilings of the n × m Grid, Cylinder, and Torus*,
        Journal of Integer Sequences 27 (2024), Article 24.6.1, Theorem 37
        (`jis-2024-24.6.1-thm-37`). -/
public theorem_wanted rectTorus_distinctTilings_burnside {T : Type*} [Fintype T]
    [DecidableEq T] (n m : ℕ) [NeZero n] [NeZero m]
    (R : Subgroup (DihedralGroup 4)) [DecidablePred (· ∈ R)] [MulAction R T]
    (hR : ∀ g ∈ R, g = .r 0 ∨ g = .r 2 ∨ g = .sr 0 ∨ g = .sr 2) :
    (Nat.card (Quot fun F F' : ZMod n × ZMod m → T =>
        ∃ v : ZMod n × ZMod m, ∃ g : R, ∀ c, F' c = g⁻¹ • F (rectCellAction n m g (c + v))) : ℚ) =
      1 / (n * m * Nat.card R) * ∑ g : R,
        (torusShiftSum n m (rectCellAction n m g) (MulAction.toPerm g : Equiv.Perm T) : ℚ)

/-- Theorem 41 (Theorem 4.2.4 of the arXiv version): for any subgroup `R` of the square group
`D₈ = ⟨r, f⟩` (Mathlib's `DihedralGroup 4`), the number of distinct tilings of the `n × n` torus
is `(1/(n²|R|)) ∑_{g ∈ R} fxpt^{ST}_g(n)`, where
`fxpt^{ST}_g(n) = torusShiftSum n n (squareCellAction n g) (g • ·)`. "Distinct" means up to the
transformations `F ↦ (c ↦ g⁻¹ • F (g · (c + v)))`, `v ∈ (ℤ/nℤ)²`, `g ∈ R`; the tile designs form an
`R`-set
(`MulAction R T`).

Source: Peter Kagey, William Keehn, *Counting Tilings of the n × m Grid, Cylinder, and Torus*,
        Journal of Integer Sequences 27 (2024), Article 24.6.1, Theorem 41
        (`jis-2024-24.6.1-thm-41`). -/
public theorem_wanted squareTorus_distinctTilings_burnside {T : Type*} [Fintype T]
    [DecidableEq T] (n : ℕ) [NeZero n]
    (R : Subgroup (DihedralGroup 4)) [DecidablePred (· ∈ R)] [MulAction R T] :
    (Nat.card (Quot fun F F' : ZMod n × ZMod n → T =>
        ∃ v : ZMod n × ZMod n, ∃ g : R, ∀ c, F' c = g⁻¹ • F (squareCellAction n g (c + v))) : ℚ) =
      1 / (n ^ 2 * Nat.card R) * ∑ g : R,
        (torusShiftSum n n (squareCellAction n g) (MulAction.toPerm g : Equiv.Perm T) : ℚ)

end

end MetaMathlibExt
